# Line-ending normalisation. See #1500.
#
# Git for Windows ships core.autocrlf=true by default, so without this file a
# Windows clone gets CRLF in the working tree even though every blob here is
# LF. Palantir Java Format (spotless:check, bound to `verify`) then rejects
# EVERY .java file before anything compiles. CI is ubuntu-latest only, so it
# never catches this — the repo simply doesn't build on Windows.
#
# `eol=lf` (not bare `text=auto`) is deliberate: it pins the WORKING TREE to LF
# regardless of the contributor's core.autocrlf setting, which is the only way
# to make the spotless gate reproducible across platforms.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files must keep CRLF — cmd.exe mis-parses LF-only .bat files.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Shell scripts must be LF everywhere, including on Windows checkouts.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary — never normalise, never diff as text.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.jar  binary
*.war  binary
*.zip  binary
*.gz   binary
*.tgz  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.xls  binary
*.xlsx binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf  binary
*.eot  binary
*.so   binary
*.dll  binary
*.dylib binary
*.keystore binary
*.p12  binary
